# Line endings: LF everywhere, including in a Windows working tree.
#
# A Windows runner checks out with `core.autocrlf=true` by default, and roughly thirty gates in
# this suite are text scans over the repository's own sources -- `anatomy_call_sites.rs` truncates
# a file at a byte offset it counts line by line, `quickstart_a_runs_everywhere.rs` splits ci.yml
# on "\n  test:\n". Under CRLF the offsets drift by one byte per line and the needles miss, so the
# gates fail on Windows while reporting something else entirely: a file with two test modules that
# has one, a ci.yml with no `test:` job that plainly has one.
#
# Normalising in each reader would be the same enumerated list those gates exist to replace, and it
# would have to be maintained by whoever adds the thirty-first. One declaration instead. `eol=lf`
# wins over `core.autocrlf`, so this holds regardless of how a contributor's git is configured, and
# `text=auto` leaves git's own binary detection in charge of the .png and .ttf files below.
#
# The three-platform matrix is what pins it: drop this line and the Windows leg goes red again,
# which is how it was found (feature 027, T115).
* text=auto eol=lf

# The documentation set (feature 023).
#
# `micold-docs` marks paths whose contents cannot affect what is built, linted, packaged or
# tested. CI skips the whole build when a change touches nothing else -- see
# `docs/development/ci-pipeline.md`.
#
# This is the single declaration. Two consumers read it, both through `git check-attr micold-docs`,
# so they cannot drift apart:
#   - scripts/classify-change.sh                          (which paths did this change touch)
#   - crates/micold-core/tests/documentation_is_not_read.rs (which paths may no test read)
#
# Pinned by scripts/tests/documentation-set.test.sh. `set` means documentation; both `unset` and
# `unspecified` mean code, so a path is code until declared otherwise. Patterns use gitignore
# syntax; negation (`!`) is not valid here, so an exception is carved out by unsetting (`-attr`)
# on a later line -- the last matching line wins.

docs/**       micold-docs
specs/**      micold-docs
/*.md         micold-docs
/LICENSE      micold-docs
/*.png        micold-docs

# Instructions the coding agent reads; nothing in the build, the suite or the package opens them.
# Scoped to `skills/` rather than all of `.claude/` because the rest of that directory is the app's
# own runtime state (`worktrees/`, local settings), which is untracked and not prose.
.claude/skills/** micold-docs

# Compiled into the binary, so a build input rather than documentation: micold-core's
# `metadata.rs` does `include_str!("../../../CHANGELOG.md")` so the app can show a "what's new"
# view with no filesystem or network access (Constitution Principle IV). Changing it changes the
# artifact, so it takes the full pipeline. Must stay after `/*.md`, which sets the attribute.
/CHANGELOG.md -micold-docs

# Read by a test, so a test input rather than documentation: feature 027's §A table is the list of
# gates the three-platform matrix is claimed to run, and
# `crates/micold-core/tests/quickstart_a_runs_everywhere.rs` compares it against `ci.yml`. If this
# stayed documentation, editing the table would skip the whole pipeline -- so the one edit the gate
# exists to catch would be the one edit it never sees. Must stay after `specs/**`, which sets the
# attribute.
/specs/027-sandboxed-daemon-runtime/quickstart.md -micold-docs
